{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fearful-halfboiled-insect","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# `read_file` silently reads to EOF when `line_end < line_start`\n\nDiscovered while root-causing [rebar:bf31-fd55-d28d-4b7a] and deliberately left out of that fix's\nscope to keep its review surface to one function.\n\n`read_file` (`src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py`) computes\n`hi = line_end if line_end and line_end >= lo else len(lines)`. An INVERTED range — `line_end`\nbelow `line_start` — therefore falls back to \"read to EOF\" (capped at `_READ_MAX_LINES`) rather\nthan reporting that the request was malformed. The agent asked for a 30-line window and silently\nreceived a 259-line one.\n\nObserved live: the looping verifier in bf31 issued\n`read_file(<path>, line_start=115, line_end=30)` **31 times**, each returning the same 11,000-char\nblob. The malformed range was not the cause of that loop, but it is the same class of defect as the\none bf31 fixed — a tool answering a request it did not actually perform, with no signal that it\nsubstituted something else.\n\nNote the deliberate, documented case that must be preserved: `line_end=0` means \"read to EOF\" and is\npart of the tool's contract.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `read_file` with `line_end < line_start` (and `line_end != 0`) returns an explicit `Error: ...`\n      naming the malformed range, instead of silently reading to EOF\n- [ ] `line_end == 0` still means \"read to EOF, capped\" — the documented behaviour is unchanged\n      (regression pinned)\n- [ ] a normal `line_start <= line_end` window is unchanged\n- [ ] the docstring states the malformed-range behaviour, since Pydantic AI passes it to the agent\n      as the tool contract (`src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.py:46`)","id":"4c2b-7b86-913e-40ee","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"read_file silently reads to EOF when line_end < line_start instead of reporting the malformed range"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785932655511315001,"uuid":"26711e82-8841-4c64-a2a5-a4a3341b20de"}